summary: System reboot verification on failure to mount root filesystem
description: |
    The purpose of this test is to verify that the system successfully reboots when
    it encounters an error or is unable to mount its designated root filesystem
    during the boot sequence. This demonstrates proper error detection and recovery
    mechanisms in the event of root filesystem access issues, preventing a stalled
    or unbootable system.

    Test Inputs:
        corrupt rootfs mount point: change related cmdline parameter
    Expected results:
        [   PASS   ] :: Command 'aboot-update -c ... $(uname -r)' (Expected 0, got 0)
        [   PASS   ] :: Command 'aboot-deploy -l aboot-$(uname -r).img' (Expected 0, got 0)
        SUT fails to reach the login prompt and test timeouts. Message expected on console:
        - [FAILED] Failed to start Mount sysroot.
    Results location:
        output.txt
        console.log
contact: Pablo Ridolfi <pridolfi@redhat.com>
id: 5c167a18-99f3-4187-a654-9dad9ad9aaed
component:
  - kernel
test: bash ./runtest.sh rootfs
framework: beakerlib
restart-on-exit-code:
    - 255
restart-max-count: 2
duration: 5m
adjust+:
    enabled: false
    when: hw_target != rcar_s4 and hw_target != ridesx4
